<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen higher, Budget to restrain.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen higher, Budget to restrain.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.30 a.m./2230 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2524.80   -1.20   DJIA  cl	7292.75 +123.22</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2541     +17   US 30yr cl	 6.89  steady</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    92.340  +0.020   Gold NY 347.65 Lon fix 348.30</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7795 (Mon 0.7783)   CRB Index cl   251.40   +1.87</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20143.51 +340.73   FTSE cl	 4669.60  +38.70</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   841.10   -0.25   NZSE40	  2309.06   +8.86</p>
<p>--------------------------(May 13)-----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen firm early but expected to slow as budget due. &quot;It will be up early but will calm down later on. People will be cautious ahead of the budget,&quot; said a Sydney dealer.</p>
